Now I understand the bug. In `host-follow.js`, `observe(options)` only updates `lastModel` when `options.model` is set. On host 0.9, `options.model` is always undefined, so `lastModel` stays at the previous session's model (`deepseek-v3.1`). The current session model is in `n.model`, but `observe` ignores `n`.

Wait, but `plugin.js` calls `host.observe(options, n)` passing n as second arg, but `observe(options)` ignores it.

The fix: `observe` should prefer the current session model from `n.model` when available, and fall back to `options.model` for old hosts.

Let me think about the semantics. "跟随宿主：记住宿主最近一次用的模型，压缩那一跳沿用它". The requirement: compressed hop model must equal current session model (n.model), and also work when old host still passes options.model.

So in session 2, n.model = 'deepseek-v3.2'. options.model is undefined. We need lastModel = 'deepseek-v3.2'.

In session 1 (old host), options.model = 'deepseek-v3.1', n.model = 'deepseek-v3.1'. Both same.

The fix: observe should read n.model primarily, fallback to options.model.

Let me modify host-follow.js:

```js
let lastModel = null

export function makeHostFollow(cfg) {
  return {
    observe(options, n) {
      const m = (n && n.model) || (options && options.model)
      if (m) lastModel = m
    },
    callConfig(options) { return { ...cfg, model: lastModel || cfg.model } },
  }
}
```

